course: dictionary
lesson: 13374
title: Words that stay with you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one you need. «The ghost haunted the old castle every night.» A ghost is not a person who visits a castle for a holiday. The clue is ghost, so haunt here means to keep visiting a place again and again.
explain: Now read this: «Ben could not forget the sad look on his dog's face. The memory kept haunting him.» A memory cannot visit a room, so haunting must mean something else: the memory stays in his mind and troubles him. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Haunting can also be an adjective that describes something. «The violin played a haunting tune that stayed in my head all week.» The tune is not a ghost. It is beautiful and sad in a way you cannot forget. Clues like tune, music and stayed in my head point to this meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Haunting» comes from the verb «haunt», which means to visit a place again and again, as a ghost does in stories.
fact: When a worry or memory keeps coming back and troubling you, it is «haunting» you.
fact: As an adjective, «haunting» means beautiful, sad or strange in a way you cannot forget, as in «a haunting melody».
fact: Check the clues first: a ghost or an old castle suggests the spooky meaning, while music or a tune suggests the beautiful, sad meaning.
exercise: «The ghost haunted the old castle every night.» What does haunted mean here? | Guarded the gate from thieves | Fell asleep in the tower | *Visited a place again and again | Painted the walls a bright colour
exercise: «Ben could not forget the sad look on his dog's face. The memory kept haunting him.» What does haunting mean here? | Packing his bags for a trip | Making him laugh out loud | *Staying in his mind and troubling him | Helping him fall asleep
exercise: «The violin played a haunting tune that stayed in my head all week.» Which word tells you the tune is beautiful and sad, not scary? | week | violin | played | *tune
test: «Her haunting song made the whole hall go silent.» What does haunting suggest? | *Beautiful and sad, so it is hard to forget | Funny and silly | Very fast, with loud drums | Boring, so people fell asleep
test: Which phrase is about a ghost visiting a place? | a haunting view of the sea | a haunting melody | a haunting memory | *haunting the castle
exam: «The children heard a haunting noise drifting down from the empty attic.» What does haunting mean here? | *Strange and eerie, hard to forget | Sweet, like a cake | Loud and cheerful | Quick and busy
